## Dry-run findings (erg check + erg init -n, read-only -- NO bug in new code)

The new code handled all 9 real stores gracefully. The dpkg compare's
manifest-absent default correctly classified every customized store's
.ergrc/AGENTS.md as "would preserve (local edits)" -- migration would clobber
nothing. Per-store, the real (pre-existing) issues a supervised migrate must
address first:

- ~/.claude/tickets: 2 closed tickets sit outside closed/ (folder hygiene);
  init -n -> preserve both assets + write manifest. HARNESS store: author
  must watch this one; do not touch unattended.
- ~/padme/tickets: erg check PASS; init -n -> preserve + manifest.
- ~/aedist-technical-report: 2 interior-header-blank warnings -> `erg migrate`.
- ~/projtmp/tickets: scratch; init -n -> create .ergrc + preserve AGENTS.md.
- ~/chemin-de-voix: 2 tickets use legacy `Tag:` -> `erg migrate` (rename to Label:).
- ~/Climate_finance: duplicate ID 0093 (real VIOLATION) + stray tools/go/*.go;
  text-only -- vendoring a binary is the owner's decision.
- ~/fuzzy-corpus, ~/cadens: legacy `%erg v1` magic line -> `erg migrate`;
  text-only adopters.

## Per-repo procedure (supervised)

For each BINARY store the owner wants on the new erg:
1. cd <repo>; `git status` -- abort if dirty (stash/commit first).
2. Refresh the traveling binary: `cp ~/git-erg/build/erg tickets/erg`
   (or build per arch). `erg version` should show role: traveling.
3. `erg migrate tickets/` if check reported a legacy-format VIOLATION
   (`%erg v1`, `Tag:`, header blanks); review `git diff`, commit separately.
4. `erg init` to refresh assets + write tickets/.erg-assets + clean orphans
   (the dpkg compare PRESERVES any local .ergrc/AGENTS.md edits -- exit 2 just
   means "skipped, nothing lost"; use `erg init --force` only to intentionally
   take the embedded defaults). Review `git diff`; commit.
5. Do NOT commit tickets/.erg-assets if the repo gitignores tickets/erg
   (manifest churns per build).
6. Optional wiring (owner opt-in): `erg install --hooks` (pre-commit),
   `erg install --push-hook` (warn-only autoarchive), `erg install
   --inject-agents` (root AGENTS.md pointer).

For each TEXT-ONLY store (Climate_finance, fuzzy-corpus, cadens): decide first
whether to adopt the binary at all. If staying text-only, just run `erg
migrate` once (with a borrowed binary) to fix the legacy format, review, and
commit -- no binary vendored.

The harness store (~/.claude/tickets) is migrated last, by the author, watching.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Read-only dry-run sweep across all 9 stores recorded (done -- above).
- [x] Author has reviewed this runbook and the per-store findings.
- [x] Each binary store the author elects is migrated (binary refreshed,
      `erg migrate` where flagged, `erg init` assets refreshed), changes
      reviewed via git diff and committed by the author.
- [x] Text-only adopters: legacy-format `erg migrate` applied where flagged
      (or a conscious decision to leave them) -- owner's call on the binary.
- [x] No store left with an `erg check` VIOLATION that `erg migrate` fixes.
